NOTE_BLOCKS = {'WG1': '<section class="cell note" id="note-WG1">\n  <div class="prompt">[lab 1]</div><div class="prose"><b>Lab book, the arithmetic of a promise.</b> Everything in this\n      development reduces to these three definitions. A <i>configuration</i> is a\n      weight function; a quorum is a set whose weight beats half the total.\n      No sets are enumerated anywhere &mdash; a quorum <i>system</i> is a\n      predicate, and &lsquo;is a quorum&rsquo; is arithmetic.</div>\n</section>', 'WG2': '<section class="cell note" id="note-WG2">\n  <div class="prompt">[lab 2]</div><div class="prose"><b>Turner\'s Lemma 2, mechanised.</b> If two configurations are at\n      scaled distance at most one &mdash; the per-node mass they move, measured\n      against common factors, is a single unit &mdash; then their strict-majority\n      families <i>frown</i>: every quorum of one meets every quorum of the other.\n      This one lemma carries every era boundary in the reincarnation schedules.</div>\n</section>', 'ER1': '<section class="cell note" id="note-ER1">\n  <div class="prompt">[lab 3]</div><div class="prose"><b>The only configuration assumption.</b> Turner\'s P1: at every era e,\n      the phase-II family of e frowns the phase-I family of e, which frowns the\n      phase-II family of e+1. Nothing else about configurations is assumed\n      anywhere in the agreement proof.</div>\n</section>', 'ER2': '<section class="cell note" id="note-ER2">\n  <div class="prompt">[lab 4]</div><div class="prose"><b>Theorem 10: per-instance agreement under reconfiguration.</b> If two\n      ballots are both chosen at instance i, they carry the same value. The proof\n      is one line of wiring: instantiate the Synod (single-decree) result per\n      instance. The era machinery discharges the Synod preconditions; P1 is the\n      only configuration fact consumed.</div>\n</section>', 'CV1': '<section class="cell note" id="note-CV1">\n  <div class="prompt">[lab 5]</div><div class="prose"><b>The casting vote.</b> When the old quorum and the new quorum meet\n      in exactly one node &mdash; the leader &mdash; that node\'s vote decides the\n      boundary. Turner uses this to cross a reconfiguration while the victim\'s\n      vote is missing presumed dead; the three-node reincarnation\'s first\n      boundary is exactly this shape.</div>\n</section>', 'RE1': '<section class="cell note" id="note-RE1">\n  <div class="prompt">[lab 6]</div><div class="prose"><b>The incarnation bump.</b> The restarted node reopens under a\n      strictly higher identity. One line of definition, one line of theorem —\n      and the entire crash-recover amnesia class becomes unrepresentable,\n      because the machine can never again run under the old identity.</div>\n</section>', 'RE2': '<section class="cell note" id="note-RE2">\n  <div class="prompt">[lab 7]</div><div class="prose"><b>The two era boundaries of the three-node schedule, discharged.</b>\n      Each is a one-liner over rung 9\'s unit-change overlap: the batch moved one\n      unit of mass, so the majorities frown. The whole of Table I\'s safety is\n      these two theorems.</div>\n</section>', 'RG1': '<section class="cell note" id="note-RG1">\n  <div class="prompt">[lab 8]</div><div class="prose"><b>Amnesia is unreachable.</b> Not &lsquo;handled&rsquo;, not\n      &lsquo;recovered&rsquo;: unreachable. Once the machine is in the bumped\n      phase, no continuation of it ever runs under the pre-bump identity again.\n      This is the formal content of &lsquo;crash-recover is unrepresentable&rsquo;\n      — and it is where the DISC\'17 bug class dies.</div>\n</section>', 'FS1': '<section class="cell note" id="note-FS1">\n  <div class="prompt">[lab 9]</div><div class="prose"><b>What a fused acknowledgement certifies.</b> One FuseOk is ONE\n      atomic vote: the sender accepted <i>every</i> packed slot. Chosen evidence\n      at a slot is then the ordinary thing — a legal quorum whose members all\n      accepted it. Fuse changes the wire, not the evidence.</div>\n</section>', 'FS2': '<section class="cell note" id="note-FS2">\n  <div class="prompt">[lab 10]</div><div class="prose"><b>The honest boundary of the fuse claim.</b> The ordinary accept\n      path admits an entry era equal to the ballot era or its successor. A shared\n      ballot spanning eras e..e+k therefore forces k ≤ 1. One datagram per era is\n      what exists and is proved; a single envelope spanning the whole six-era\n      swap owes the multi-era refinement the addendum names. This theorem is the\n      arithmetic that keeps the paper honest.</div>\n</section>', 'FS3': '<section class="cell note" id="note-FS3">\n  <div class="prompt">[lab 11]</div><div class="prose"><b>The Telescoping Theorem.</b> One response set acknowledges the\n      whole batch; if it is a quorum at the first transition and eligibility is\n      preserved at each step, it is a quorum at every transition of the\n      schedule. Lamport ran the same induction in Paxos Made Simple §2.5 —\n      &lsquo;using the same proposal number for all instances&rsquo;. Here it is\n      kernel-checked, with the preservation hypothesis explicit.</div>\n</section>', 'FS4': '<section class="cell note" id="note-FS4">\n  <div class="prompt">[lab 12]</div><div class="prose"><b>The negative control that earns the hypothesis.</b> The\n      equal-total swap (1,2,1,2)→(2,1,2,1): the response set {B,D} is a majority\n      before and a minority after. Preservation is not decoration — drop it and\n      telescoping is false. A proof whose load-bearing hypotheses are not\n      exercised by a failing case is not a proof, it is a decoration.</div>\n</section>', 'RS1': '<section class="cell note" id="note-RS1">\n  <div class="prompt">[lab 13]</div><div class="prose"><b>The final composition.</b> five_safe: for a five-voter cluster\n      running the two committed reconfiguration eras, under every view schedule\n      satisfying the history contract — agreement, the replacement weights, the\n      eviction of the old identity from voting authority, and identity\n      non-reuse. Four conjuncts, each discharged by a rung already climbed.\n      This is the theorem the whole ladder exists to state.</div>\n</section>'}

